  "query_preview": "..Dry southwest aloft today across southeast Arizona\nwith weak troughiness off to our west. Gradients remain tight enough \nto result in breezy conditions this afternoon, especially from \nTucson south and eastward with sustained winds of 15-25 mph and \ngusts up to 35 mph. This will result in near critical fire weather \nconditions in Santa Cruz and Cochise Counties where the strongest \nwinds will be with elevated fire weather conditions elsewhere. \nTemperatures will be a couple of degrees cooler than yesterday but \nstill about 3 to 7 degrees above normal. \n\nFriday: The area will generally be between weather systems with just \na bit of afternoon gustiness to around 20 mph. Little change in \ntemperatures.\n\nSaturday: As the next trough approaches winds will tick up slightly \ninto the 10-20 mph range sustained with gusts up to 30 mph. Little \nchange in temperatures.\n\nSunday/Monday: Ensembles are in good agreement that a dry trough \nwill swing through the region. This will result in breezy to locally \nwindy conditions area-wide Sunday and then trending more towards \neastern areas on Monday. Still time to nail down specifics depending \non the strength/timing of the trough as it moves through but for now \nwe're looking at sustained winds of 15-30 mph with gusts 35-45 mph \nSunday for all of our forecast area and Monday south and east of \nTucson. The combination of these strong winds and low relative \nhumidity will result in fire weather concerns during this period and \npotential need for headlines on later shifts. The trough will bring \nin a bit more cooling with highs lowering to seasonable levels \nSunday and Monday. \n\nTuesday/Wednesday: The bulk of the troughiness will have exited the \nregion allowing for winds to drop back down to typical levels, with \ntemperatures nudging back to above normal levels by Wednesday.",
